    "q-149505": {
      "dom_id": "step-q149505",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Let $f(x)$ be negative and strictly increasing for $x\\in [0,1],$ and differentiable for $x\\in (0,1).$ Suppose we approximate the area under the curve $y=g(x)=({x}^{2}-2)\\cdot f(x)$ over the interval $[0,1]$ using a right Riemann sum. Given that $g(x)>0,$ which of the following statements must be true?\n\nI. ${f}^{′}(x)>0$\n\nII. ${g}^{′}(x)>0$\n\nIII. The Riemann sum underestimates the true area.",
      "worked_solution": "We're given that $g(x)=({x}^{2}-2)\\cdot f(x)>0.$ Now, recall the following:\n\n- If $g(x)$ is strictly increasing, the right Riemann sum gives an *overestimate* of the area under the curve $y=g(x).$\n\n- If $g(x)$ is strictly decreasing, the right Riemann sum gives an *underestimate* of the area under the curve $y=g(x).$\n\nLet's now consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $f(x)$ is strictly increasing, we have ${f}^{′}(x)>0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Differentiating $g(x)=({x}^{2}-2)\\cdot f(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{2}-2)^{′}\\cdot f(x)+({x}^{2}-2)\\cdot {f}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =2x\\cdot f(x)+({x}^{2}-2)\\cdot {f}^{′}(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x)$ is negative and strictly increasing over the interval $(0,1),$ we have \n\n$$\n2x>0,\\,f(x)<0,\\,{x}^{2}-2<0,\\,{f}^{′}(x)>0.\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)={{2x}_{⏟}}_{>0}\\cdot {{f(x)}_{⏟}}_{<0}+{{({x}^{2}-2)}_{⏟}}_{<0}\\cdot {{{f}^{′}(x)}_{⏟}}_{>0}={{2x\\cdot f(x)}_{⏟}}_{<0}+\\,{{{x}^{2}\\cdot {f}^{′}(x)}_{⏟}}_{<0}<0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${g}^{′}(x)<0,$ the function $g(x)$ is strictly decreasing. Therefore, the right Riemann sum gives an *underestimate* of the area under the curve $y=({x}^{2}-2)\\cdot f(x).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-149505-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I and III only",
              "html": "I and III only"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-149505-b",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I and II only",
              "html": "I and II only"
            },
            {
              "option": "c",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-149505-c",
